{
  "abstract": "We re-execute the Route A geometric overlap ansatz against the selected multi-loop gauge-profile targets of Paper I. In its stated dimensionless normalization, the effective round-sphere lens base and isotropic compact Heisenberg nilmanifold can be retargeted analytically: the squared lens amplitude-radius product equals 0.2555137 times the circle coordinate R1, and the nil coefficient equals 0.9948493 times R1. The spectral lower bounds remain above the assumed dimensionless admissibility floor. This establishes a calibrated representative in the declared auxiliary ansatz. It does not prove that the full lens space reduces to the spherical model, identify that representative with the q79 Fu-Yau compactification, select a geometry uniquely by MTT, or predict the gauge couplings without their measured inputs. The shared circle is common phase and holonomy data, not an additional coordinate factor multiplying Lens and Nil.",
